IMPORT prelude

-- Accountants Act 2004 (Singapore) -- what only a public accountant may do (s 2), who may register (s 10), the
-- accounting corporation's duties to clients (s 24) and its directors' collective liability (s 25), disciplinary sanctions
-- (s 52), holding out (s 56), fees for unregistered work (s 57), and employing disqualified persons (s 59).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/AA2004.txt
-- (amendments to Act 24 of 2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 35 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository, spread thinly; most name it to say who
-- may audit. SCOPED to the reserved activity and the professional's exposure. Not encoded: administration and the
-- Oversight Committee, registration procedure, accounting entity approvals and governance, practice monitoring and quality
-- reviews (Parts 5 and 5A), the complaints and inquiry procedure, and the transitional provisions.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Accountants Act 2004 -- public accountants`

§§ `2 -- the reserved activity`

-- s 2(1): "'public accountancy services' means the AUDIT and reporting on financial statements and the doing of any other
-- acts that are REQUIRED BY ANY WRITTEN LAW to be done by a public accountant".
--
-- The reserved field is narrow. Bookkeeping, tax returns, management accounts, valuations and advisory work are not
-- public accountancy services unless some written law requires a public accountant for them. Anyone may do them for a fee.
DECLARE Service IS ONE OF
    `a statutory audit of financial statements`
    `an act a written law reserves to a public accountant`
    `bookkeeping`
    `preparing tax returns`
    `management accounts`
    `business valuation advice`

GIVEN `the service` IS A Service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is a public accountancy service` IF
    CONSIDER `the service`
    WHEN `a statutory audit of financial statements` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an act a written law reserves to a public accountant` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `10 -- who may register`

-- s 10(1): an individual who "(a) has attained 21 years of age; and (b) satisfies the prescribed requirements relating to
-- (i) qualifications; (ii) practical experience; and (iii) membership in any professional accountancy body" is ENTITLED,
-- on paying the fee, to be registered. s 11(5): but the Oversight Committee MAY refuse one not of good reputation or
-- character, engaged in an inconsistent business, or otherwise unfit.
DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `meets the prescribed qualifications, experience and membership` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of good reputation and character and otherwise fit` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant meets section 10` IF
        `the applicant`'s `age` AT LEAST 21
    AND `the applicant`'s `meets the prescribed qualifications, experience and membership`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Oversight Committee may refuse` IF
        NOT `the applicant meets section 10` `the applicant`
    OR  NOT `the applicant`'s `of good reputation and character and otherwise fit`

§§ `24, 25 -- the firm and its directors`

-- s 24: an accounting corporation or LLP has "the same rights and [is] subject to the same fiduciary, confidential and
-- ethical requirements with respect to each client ... that exist at law with respect to a public accountant and his or
-- her client".
-- s 25(2): the directors or partners who are public accountants "shall be JOINTLY liable to disciplinary proceedings" if
-- the business is conducted in a way warranting discipline "and where such conduct CANNOT BE ATTRIBUTED to the act or
-- omission of any particular public accountant".
--
-- Where no one can be blamed, everyone can be disciplined.
GIVEN `the firm's conduct warrants discipline` IS A BOOLEAN, `attributable to a particular accountant` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a director or partner who is a public accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is liable to discipline for the firm's conduct` IF
        `the firm's conduct warrants discipline`
    AND NOT `attributable to a particular accountant`
    AND `is a director or partner who is a public accountant`

§§ `52 -- discipline`

-- s 52(1): grounds include (a) conviction anywhere of an offence involving fraud, dishonesty or moral turpitude; (b) one
-- implying a defect of character; (c) improper or dishonourable conduct; (d) an incompatible business; (e) a director
-- failing to take reasonable steps to stop the firm's misconduct; (f) providing services through an unapproved company or
-- LLP; (g) practising while the firm lacks professional indemnity insurance.
-- s 52(2): the Oversight Committee may (a) cancel registration; (b) suspend "for a period not exceeding 2 YEARS"; (c)
-- impose conditions up to 2 years; (d) impose "a penalty not exceeding $10,000"; (e) censure; (f) require an undertaking.
--
-- The financial penalty for an auditor is capped at $10,000 and suspension at 2 years -- against $100,000 and 3 years for
-- a doctor (Medical Registration Act s 59D) and $100,000 and 5 years for a lawyer (Legal Profession Act s 83).
DECLARE Sanction HAS
    `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER
    `penalty` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the sanction` IS A Sanction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sanction is within section 52(2)` IF
        `the sanction`'s `months of suspension` AT MOST 24
    AND `the sanction`'s `penalty` AT MOST 10000

DECLARE Profession IS ONE OF
    `public accountant`
    `medical practitioner`
    `advocate and solicitor`

GIVEN `the profession` IS A Profession
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum disciplinary penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the profession`
    WHEN `public accountant` THEN 10000
    WHEN `medical practitioner` THEN 100000
    WHEN `advocate and solicitor` THEN 100000

GIVEN `the profession` IS A Profession
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum suspension in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the profession`
    WHEN `public accountant` THEN 2
    WHEN `medical practitioner` THEN 3
    WHEN `advocate and solicitor` THEN 5

§§ `56, 57 -- the unregistered`

-- s 56(1): a person not registered must not practise as a public accountant, hold out as one, or use any title tending to
-- convey that impression. (1A): nor a suspended one, during suspension. (2): a body corporate not approved must not provide
-- public accountancy services or use "Public Accounting Corporation" or "PAC". Penalty: $5,000 or 12 months; repeat $10,000
-- or 2 years.
-- s 57(1): "a person is NOT ENTITLED TO RECOVER any expenses or remuneration for ... any public accountancy services ...
-- unless the person ... is" a public accountant or approved entity. (3): "Any person who CONTRAVENES subsection (1) shall be
-- guilty of an offence" -- $5,000 or 12 months.
--
-- Subsection (1) states a disentitlement, not a prohibition: it says what a person may not recover, not what a person must
-- not do. What it is to "contravene" a disentitlement -- suing for the fee? receiving it? -- the text does not say.
GIVEN `registered or approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `provided a public accountancy service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may recover the fee` IF
    `registered or approved` OR NOT `provided a public accountancy service`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 57(1) states a prohibition one can contravene` IF
    FALSE

GIVEN `uses PAC or Public Accounting Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN, `is an approved accounting corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the name contravenes section 56(2)` IF
    `uses PAC or Public Accounting Corporation` AND NOT `is an approved accounting corporation`

§§ `59 -- employing disqualified persons`

-- s 59(1): without the Oversight Committee's consent, a public accountant or accounting entity must not, in connection with
-- public accountancy services, employ or remunerate any person who TO ITS KNOWLEDGE (a) is an undischarged bankrupt; (b)
-- had registration suspended or cancelled; or (c) "has been convicted of an offence ... and sentenced to imprisonment for a
-- term of not less than 12 months or to a fine of not less than $5,000".
--
-- (c) has no time limit and no restriction to offences of dishonesty: a 20-year-old conviction for any offence with a
-- $5,000 fine still bars employment without consent.
DECLARE Hire HAS
    `known undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `known suspended or cancelled accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `known conviction with 12 months' jail or a $5,000 fine` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Oversight Committee consented` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the hire` IS A Hire
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hire contravenes section 59` IF
        NOT `the hire`'s `the Oversight Committee consented`
    AND (    `the hire`'s `known undischarged bankrupt`
         OR  `the hire`'s `known suspended or cancelled accountant`
         OR  `the hire`'s `known conviction with 12 months' jail or a $5,000 fine`)
